Package: OligoMetProfiler
Type: Package
Title: Theoretical Metabolite Libraries, Charge Envelopes, and MS/MS
    Fragment Ions for Therapeutic Oligonucleotides
Version: 1.0.0
Date: 2026-08-22
Authors@R: person("Nishikant", "Wase",
    email = "nishikant.wase@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
    comment = "Author and developer; Research Scientist, Thermo Fisher
    Scientific. An independent personal project, not a Thermo Fisher
    Scientific product.")
Description: In-silico metabolite identification for therapeutic
    oligonucleotides (antisense, siRNA, and related modalities).
    Generates theoretical metabolite libraries (exonuclease truncations
    and endonuclease internal fragments), molecular formulas,
    monoisotopic and average masses, negative-ESI charge envelopes,
    isotope patterns, phosphorothioate oxidation series, MS/MS fragment
    ions, and PRM inclusion lists for any sequence built from DNA, RNA,
    2'-O-methyl, 2'-fluoro, MOE, cEt, or LNA chemistry with mixed PO/PS
    backbones. Exports a multi-sheet Excel workbook, an HTML report,
    MGF/MSP spectral libraries, and targeted mass lists for the Thermo
    Orbitrap Exploris Method Editor; optionally matches the library
    against mzML/mzXML or peak-list data. A bundled Python pipeline adds
    parallel charge-envelope deconvolution of many raw files at once,
    MS2 confirmation of matched hits, and a statistics suite comparing
    each confirmed metabolite across experimental groups or a time
    series. Four approved drugs
    (nusinersen, inotersen, patisiran, givosiran) ship as worked
    examples, two of which anchor the formula engine's regression tests.
    A Shiny dashboard (run_app()) and command-line drivers wrap the same
    engine. FOR RESEARCH USE ONLY: not for diagnostic, clinical, or
    regulatory submission use. All outputs are computed predictions that
    must be confirmed experimentally; provided without warranty (see
    DISCLAIMER.md).
